# GuardTalk repo-root build / dependency output trees.
# Added by T-EXCISE-REPO-IGNORE-GAP (2026-09-25) — repo hygiene, prevention half.
#
# WHY THESE PATTERNS ARE ROOT-ANCHORED (`/...`) AND NOT `out*/` / `*.stale-*` bare:
#   This repo tracks a REAL fixture tree at
#     docs/qa/fixtures/un-excised/out/target/product/<device>/...
#   An unanchored `out*/` would match that nested path. Git itself never hides
#   already-tracked files, but ripgrep-based agent search DOES apply .gitignore
#   patterns blindly — so an unanchored rule would silently hide tracked fixture
#   files (radio.img / installed-files-vendor.txt / ...) from every future grep.
#   Anchoring to the repository root keeps those tracked fixtures visible.
#
# SCOPE / HONEST LIMIT:
#   The stale `out_adevtool_deps.stale-*` tree that caused the ~95% grep false
#   hits lives at the WORKSPACE ROOT, which is an Android `repo` checkout with
#   NO `.git` and is OUTSIDE this repository. This file therefore CANNOT exclude
#   it. See .agent-comm/evidence/T-EXCISE-REPO-IGNORE-GAP/ and the per-task
#   report for the root-scope gap and the recommended root-level ignore file.

# --- Emulator / adevtool dependency output trees (repository root only) ---
/out/
/out_adevtool_deps/
/out_adevtool_deps.stale-*/

# --- Stale snapshots (e.g. *.stale-<timestamp>/) at repository root only ---
/*.stale-*/
